            <ArticleTitle>[Pain, the elderly and verbal communication disorders].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>24-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The prevalence of pain increases with age and multiple pathologies. Care procedures and movement are often triggers: dressings, injections, perfusions, washing, changes, transfers, walking, meals, etc. Which tools should be used when speech is lacking? What are the challenges in geriatrics for the patient and the caregivers? How should we orient our observations or behavioural disorders in terms of pain, anxiety or dementia?</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
